    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The presence of those markers is enforced by [@typescript-eslint/explicit-member-accessibility](https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/blob/master/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/explicit-member-accessibility.md).\r\n\r\nI think they are useful since they are protecting us (and some consumers) to use private methods. They also could potentially make our lives easier if we migrate to native [private methods](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-private-methods) in the future.\r\n\r\nBut for consumers that do not use TS I think we should also prefix the method names with a `_` since it is common to indicate a private property/method like this in JavaScript (this could be enforced by a tool like ESLint).\r\n",
    "commit_id": "611090bff85eb37e8b5f8d99dbc65d2cb3561fa6",
    "created_at": "2019-05-07T15:08:30Z",
